[
    {
        "slide_number": 1,
        "title": "Unlock Your Learning Potential",
        "bullets": [
            "Many students struggle with **information overload** and retaining what they study.",
            "Effective study skills are not just about effort, but about **smart strategies**.",
            "This session will explore practical techniques to enhance your **comprehension and recall**."
        ]
    },
    {
        "slide_number": 2,
        "title": "Active Learning: Beyond Rereading",
        "bullets": [
            "**Passive reading** often leads to poor retention; your brain needs to engage.",
            "Try **summarizing in your own words** after each section, or explaining concepts aloud.",
            "**Question yourself** as you go: 'What's the main idea here?' or 'How does this connect to what I already know?'",
            "Create **flashcards or mind maps** to actively process and organize information."
        ]
    },
    {
        "slide_number": 3,
        "title": "Spaced Repetition & Interleaving",
        "bullets": [
            "**Spaced repetition** involves reviewing material at increasing intervals to strengthen memory.",
            "Instead of cramming, schedule **short, regular review sessions** over days or weeks.",
            "**Interleaving** means mixing different subjects or topics during a single study session.",
            "This technique helps your brain **discriminate between concepts** and improves long-term retention."
        ]
    },
    {
        "slide_number": 4,
        "title": "Conclusion: Study Smarter, Not Harder",
        "bullets": [
            "Adopt **active learning** to deeply engage with your material.",
            "Utilize **spaced repetition** for robust, long-lasting memory.",
            "Integrate **interleaving** to build stronger connections between topics.",
            "These strategies empower you to **master complex subjects** and achieve academic success."
        ]
    }
]

